o distance is excluded.\n\n4. The GPS trace is schema-impaired but policy-clean, and both must be said. EV-GPS-00107 carries the pre-pass issues GPS_DRIFT and IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED (a 331.8 m multipath jump at 21:44:57 in the Raffles Place urban canyon, implying impossible speeds) and a weight_multiplier of 0.30, which POL-GEN-02(3) requires me to name. For policy purposes under POL-RD-07 it is clean: no gap over 90 s (largest gap 0.0 s), no jump over 500 m (largest 331.8 m), no sampling interval over 30 s (10 s). POL-RD-07's consequences and POL-RD-10(3) are not engaged, the deviation may be established on the trace, and the finding survives the 0.30 discount.\n\n5. Confidence. A 0.30 weight would cap confidence if the trace were the only carrier of the deciding fact. It is not. The chat log EV-CHAT-00107 (weight 1.0) is a contemporaneous record made from inside the disputed window and independently supports the deviation, and the driver's own account concedes the route. POL-GEN-02(2) takes the MAXIMUM where independent artifacts carry the fact, so the cap is 1.00, not 0.30, and POL-RD-10(1) is not triggered. I do not rely on the fare breakdown's 17.60 km (called 'an independent billing record' in its admissibility note) or on the trip record's 17.6 km: under POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-07(ii) each is a copy of the same trace measurement and corroborates nothing. That argument of the rider's fails in its reasoning even though the no-escalation outcome it seeks is right.\n\n6. The refund (POL-RD-02). fare_model is METERED and quoted_fare_sgd is null, so POL-RD-11 does not apply. recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 14.0 + 0.28 x 24.0) x 1.35 + 0.80 = 29.177. charged_total = 36.60. Refund = 36.60 - 29.177 = 7.423, rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05 = 7.45. The 1.35 surge multiplier is read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier and is kept. There is no ERP (0.00), no fixed surcharge, no waiting fee and no promo discount. 7.45 is 20.3% of the charge: above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 7.45, not the SGD 12.00 claimed.\n\n7. Burden and profiles. The rider's counters deviation_claims_60d (5) and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated (1), with an excess below 30%, make POL-RD-08 require corroboration beyond the trace; that corroboration is supplied by the driver's own statement admitting the route, one of the sources POL-RD-07(ii) names, so the claim is proven and her history is not used to deny it. Every other profile field (rating, lifetime counters, cancellation rates, prior flags) is context only under POL-GEN-01 and is used for nothing.\n\n8. Effect. The monetary effect (SGD 7.45) does not exceed the SGD 8.00 execution threshold and is executed on issue under POL-GEN-05. If either party can add a record-type artifact - for example a traffic advisory for the CTE covering 21:13-21:47 on 18 July - POL-GEN-04 allows one appeal within 30 days."
